    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d618">

                <pb facs="1137" n="1121" sameAs="frus:frus1950v04/pg1121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">261.1122/3–1150: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Barbour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-03-11T14:00:00+03:00">March 11, 1950—2
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>815. Embtel 706, February 28.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d618-f1"/> Embassy letter to
                    Anna Spiegel, notifying her MFA’s decision to permit her to depart USSR, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> February 28 returned undelivered with
                    postal notation: “Addressee departed destination unknown.”</p>
                <p>Of the five persons allegedly permitted to depart USSR, Henry Blacha, Valentina
                    and Vladimir Kazun have “stated” refusal to return USA and desire to remain
                    USSR, Spiegel has not been located, and Adele Sagatas has not replied to Embassy
                    letter.</p>
                <p>Suggest relatives in USA be notified that Embassy is doing everything possible to
                    effect repatriation of these persons but that good faith on part of MFA in this
                    matter is doubted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Barbour</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
